    }
   ],
   "gap": "Durrett Exercise 3.3.24 (PTE5 printed p.143 = PDF p.151) asks to show nu_k^{1/k} -> Lambda, 'so the assumption of Theorem 3.3.26 holds if Lambda < infinity'. The handbook proves the limit and compact determinacy (body 451-463, annex 1038-1077) but never writes the consequence clause: that Lambda < infinity gives the Theorem 3.3.26 growth hypothesis limsup_k m_{2k}^{1/(2k)}/(2k) < infinity (m_{2k}^{1/(2k)} = nu_{2k}^{1/(2k)} -> Lambda < infinity, so the ratio tends to zero). Owed: state and prove this consequence clause, completing Exercise 3.3.24."
